      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-coset-proof",
      "title": "Existence of the signed valuation, middle coset and radical coordinate",
      "statement": "In the local unramified unitary case n=m+2, fix a lift of each element of G_m/K_m. For every g in G_n there are a∈ℤ, a middle coset y and u in the upper block radical such that g=M(a,y)uk with k integral, where the two outer diagonal entries of M are ϖ^a and ϖ^(−a).",
      "definitions": [
        "K_n is the group of integral unitary matrices for the anti-diagonal Hermitian form.",
        "The choice of representative of y is fixed before the radical coordinate is tested."
      ],
